desc:ChannelView Modulators
author: Tim Shadgett
noindex: true

/*
  TS_CV_Modulators.jsfx -- ChannelView's macros and modulators for one track.
  Set up and shown by ChannelView's Macros and Modulators panels; every
  setting here is a parameter, so each can have an automation lane.

  Controls take their value from this plugin through REAPER's own
  parameter links (Parameter modulation > Link from MIDI or FX parameter).
  Audio and MIDI pass through untouched.

  Parameters (0-based, as REAPER numbers them):
    0-15      Macro 1-16
    16 + 22*(n-1) + k   Modulator n's field k:
       0  Type
       1  Output
       2  Output bipolar
       3  Depth
       4  Smooth
       5  LFO Shape
       6  LFO Sync
       7  LFO Rate (sync)
       8  LFO Rate (Hz)
       9  LFO Phase
      10  Follower Source
      11  Follower Attack
      12  Follower Release
      13  Follower Floor
      14  Follower Ceiling
      15  Follower Gate
      16  MIDI Source
      17  MIDI Channel
      18  MIDI CC
      19  MIDI Low note
      20  MIDI High note
      21  MIDI Hold
  Output is 0..1 from rest (Depth scales it); Output bipolar swings
  round 0.5 (Depth scales the swing), for controls driven both ways.
    192 + 6*(n-1) + 3*(s-1) + k   Modulator n's source s (of 2), field k:
       0  Source   0 none, 1-16 Macro 1-16, 17-24 Modulator 1-8
       1  Target   which setting it moves (THE MATRIX below), + 100 x the
                   macro's choices when the target is a switch
       2  Amount   a setting's share of its knob's range, -1..1; for a
                   switch, the setting by choice, one decimal digit each

  THE MATRIX (ChannelView 2.1.2). Each modulator's settings can be moved
  by two sources: a macro, or another modulator. Worked out here, at the
  top of every block -- the moved settings are written over the knobs'
  for this block and put back at its end, so the knobs (and their lanes)
  keep their own values. A modulator moved by another uses that one's
  output from the block before, so two can move each other.
  Targets: 1 Depth, 2 Rate (Hz, or the synced rate in whole steps),
  3 Phase, 4 Smooth, 5 Attack, 6 Release, 7 Floor, 8 Ceiling, 9 Low
  note, 10 High note -- each moved within its knob's own scale -- and
  the switches, from a button or dropdown macro only: 11 Shape, 12 Sync,
  13 Follower source, 14 Gate, 15 Hold. A switch's Amount holds, in its
  decimal digits from the lowest, the setting for each of the macro's
  choices (0 its own, 1.. the setting + 1), up to six; the choices count
  is the Target's hundreds.
  Projects saved before 2.1.2 load with all of these at 0: nothing moved,
  every link and lane where it was.

  The idea of macros and modulators living in the chain, linked by
  REAPER's parameter modulation, comes from Saxmand's FX Modulator
  Linking (Jesper Ankarfeldt), with thanks.
*/

